(EXP-44: `and` is true only when both conditions are true.
 Also covers: EXP-45 `or` is true when either is true, EXP-46 `not` is true
 when its condition is false.
 All four rows of each truth table are recorded, so a leaf asserting on a
 logical join has the whole table hand-verified rather than the one row that
 happened to be tried.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-44.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   and TT true
   and TF false
   and FT false
   and FF false
   or TT true
   or TF true
   or FT true
   or FF false
   not T false
   not F true
)
a boolean called affirmed is true.
a boolean called denied is false.
If affirmed and affirmed then, Print "and TT true". Otherwise, Print "and TT false".
If affirmed and denied then, Print "and TF true". Otherwise, Print "and TF false".
If denied and affirmed then, Print "and FT true". Otherwise, Print "and FT false".
If denied and denied then, Print "and FF true". Otherwise, Print "and FF false".
If affirmed or affirmed then, Print "or TT true". Otherwise, Print "or TT false".
If affirmed or denied then, Print "or TF true". Otherwise, Print "or TF false".
If denied or affirmed then, Print "or FT true". Otherwise, Print "or FT false".
If denied or denied then, Print "or FF true". Otherwise, Print "or FF false".
If not affirmed then, Print "not T true". Otherwise, Print "not T false".
If not denied then, Print "not F true". Otherwise, Print "not F false".
